<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/royce-oneale/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/royce-oneale/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Royce O’Neale’s Salary at Charlotte in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"O’Neale earns $10.88m in 2026-27, seventh on the Charlotte payroll. It rises from $10.13m last season. His career earnings come to $70.19m across ten seasons. The salary is 6.73% of Charlotte’s $161.69m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Royce O’Neale Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"One season remains after this one, worth $11.63m and fully guaranteed. He reaches unrestricted free agency in the summer of 2028 at 35, which is late enough that the next contract is likely to be a one-year deal at the minimum or close to it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Royce O’Neale Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $10.88m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Are the Terms of Royce O’Neale’s Contract?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"O’Neale signed a four-year contract worth $42m on July 6, 2024, fully guaranteed, under Bird rights. Phoenix signed it and Charlotte took it on. The money rises each season, from $9.38m to $12.38m, and it carries no options at either end. He reaches unrestricted free agency in 2028 at 35."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Royce O’Neale’s Net Worth in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"O’Neale’s net worth is estimated at around $28m, derived from his $70.19m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. He reached the NBA at 24, two years after leaving Baylor, and his first season paid $816k. Every season since has paid more than the one before, except 2024-25."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Is Royce O’Neale Paid $10.88m?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"O’Neale is paid $10.88m because he is a wing defender who shoots threes in volume, and that combination holds its price into a player’s thirties. He earns slightly more than Kon Knueppel, the fourth pick in the 2025 draft, who is twelve years younger."}}]}</script>
